From daaa88e31e286d76d6423ad606d0be5d9a17b598 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <claude-edit@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 11:52:32 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(permissions): describe what a command does in plain
 language
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Under the approval panel, show one or two sentences saying what the
command does and what deserves a second look. The panel and its command
line are unchanged.

- deterministic and local: rules, not a model, so it cannot be steered by
  the injection that wrote the command
- never says a command is safe; says so when it cannot describe part of
  it or when the effect depends on a script
- hidden or look-alike characters are shown as ⟦U+XXXX⟧
- Settings: explain that without an OS sandbox the approval prompt is the
  only control (shown only where commands run unsandboxed)
